transition function:
- insufficient_evidence + aggregate: if _suspension_required -> suspended (persist_state, set_cooldown); elif sample_count >= min_samples -> normal (persist_state); else unchanged () . guard: state not suspended/probing; target state; action.
- insufficient_evidence + cooldown_expired: returns state,() (only suspended/probing handled). ignored.
- insufficient_evidence + probe_success: state==probing_recovery required -> false -> unchanged.
- insufficient_evidence + probe_failure: same.
- normal + aggregate: _suspension_required -> suspended; else unchanged (state != insufficient_evidence so no normal transition). 
- normal + cooldown_expired: unchanged.
- normal + probe_success: unchanged.
- normal + probe_failure: unchanged.
- suspended + aggregate: if retry_after_until is not None and (cooldown_until None or retry_after > cooldown) -> suspended (persist_state, set_cooldown) i.e. extend. else unchanged. Note _suspension_required not evaluated while suspended.
- suspended + cooldown_expired: if cooldown_until not None and <= now -> probing_recovery (persist, claim). else unchanged.
- suspended + probe_success: requires probing_recovery -> unchanged (probe outcomes arrive via probe_* but from suspended no-op).
- suspended + probe_failure: unchanged.
- probing_recovery + aggregate: state in ("suspended","probing_recovery") -> returns state, () (no change; the suspended branch requires state=="suspended").
- probing_recovery + cooldown_expired: if probe_expires_at <= now -> probing_recovery (persist, claim_probe_slot). else unchanged.
- probing_recovery + probe_success: _live_probe -> normal (persist, release, reset_window); else unchanged.
- probing_recovery + probe_failure: _live_probe -> suspended (persist, release, set_cooldown); else unchanged.

